rough `signature_findings` to either verdict, so the new classification is unpinned.\n\n## Approach\nAdd tests that write a real op-cert SIGNATURE event, corrupt it so `verify_opcert_record` returns `invalid` (e.g. a malformed or tampered envelope), and separately produce `key_not_valid_at_era` if the verifier can reach it from a store fixture; assert `signature_findings` returns exactly one MAJOR finding naming the ticket. If `key_not_valid_at_era` is unreachable from the op-cert verify path, record that finding on this ticket and drop it from the mapping instead of keeping dead classification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A test asserts an `invalid` op-cert yields one MAJOR `[SIGNATURE]` finding from `signature_findings`.\n- [ ] `key_not_valid_at_era` is either pinned by a test the same way or removed from the mapping with the reason recorded here.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["test-gap"],"ticket_id":"5a7a-9aa9-73e4-4125","ticket_type":"task","title":"Test signature_findings maps a real op-cert's invalid / key_not_valid_at_era verdicts to MAJOR findings","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["24fa03f1-d128-43b9-8534-54496e07edea","d680ebc7-b6ce-492a-8ede-2cdbec730a3a"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792380020446633001,"uuid":"43129783-790e-4ec7-ab15-ff6bd55920b5"}